<Axiom id="AX_CAP_5">Five critic results is the hard automatic cap. At the fifth result — regardless
      of sensor verdict — the operator must dispose the cycle before readiness or another dispatch. If that
      round made no edits, the choices are `CLEAN`, `CONTINUE THROUGH ROUND N` with an explicit higher cap,
      or `RESTART: reason`; if it made edits, CLEAN is unavailable because the changed bytes have not been
      reviewed, so only CONTINUE or RESTART are offered. A raised cap behaves identically when reached. The
    sensor cannot authorize continuation, and continuation is never readiness.</Axiom>

<Contract id="FEASIBILITY_STATE_FORMAT">
      `FeasibilityState` is the validated fold of `sdd-scaffold-feasibility/v1` events in the open
      session journal. Write one JSON event to
      `.claude/tmp/sdd-scaffold-feasibility-event.json`, call the declared `sdd-session feasibility`
      ToolCall, and follow its single `NEXT=` instruction. A rejected event changes neither session nor
      payload. The CLI, not the model, owns sequence, result count, cap, retained-worker, target-hash,
      fork, Gate 2, and restart transitions.

      Every event has the exact key set `{schema,cycle,seq,event,payload}`; JSON key order is immaterial.
      A cycle begins with `opened {targets,fallbackUsed:false,resultCount:0,activeCap:5}`, then records
      `worker-state {availability,workerSession,fallbackUsed}` before its first `sensor-result`.
      Each critic response is recorded exactly once as
      `sensor-result {resultCount,verdict,changes,targets}` before any correction, re-dispatch, Gate 2,
      or cap decision. A no-change product/toolchain fork additionally carries `fork` with verdict
      `NEW_FORK`. Ticket mutations use `target-refreshed {targets,changedTickets}` before re-dispatch.

      At the active cap, record the operator's exact
      `operator-disposition {resultCount,disposition}`: `CLEAN`, `CONTINUE THROUGH ROUND N`, or
      `RESTART: reason`. RESTART authorizes a new cycle whose `opened` resets count/cap/worker state.
      Gate 2 records `gate2-choice {choices,changedTickets}`; non-empty changed tickets must be refreshed
      and reviewed by the retained critic before `closed {}`. A NEW_FORK reaches Gate 2 as an unresolved
      delta and cannot auto-approve itself. The regular terminal `sdd-session close` alone removes the
      session scratch.
    </Contract>

<Contract id="FEASIBILITY_CRITIC_CONTEXT">
      A green `feasibilityGate` emits one `critic-context:` JSON line with schema
      `sdd-scaffold-critic-context/v1`. It is the semantic critic's authoritative mechanical input:
      ticket paths/dependencies, clean-HEAD package facts, global package ownership, per-phase
      targets/profiles/ladders/bootstrap edges, Verification routing, command proof, coverage, and
      deterministic schema gaps. The first dispatch carries it unchanged. After ticket bytes change,
      the same gate refreshes it and the same-session delta carries changed tickets plus the new exact
      value. If a semantic conclusion needs a fact absent from the context — including an external
      generator's real output contract — return `TOOL_CONTRACT_MISSING: <fact> — <needed-for>` instead
      of replacing evidence with an implementation guess.
    </Contract>

